    "description": "Leatherstocking Gas Company is a regulated natural gas utility that extends service into underserved areas of New York and Pennsylvania. It serves residential, commercial, and small industrial customers through an asset-heavy local distribution model built around owned pipeline infrastructure and utility franchises. Company history materials state that the business began as a 50/50 partnership in 2010 in New York and 2011 in Pennsylvania, and that it began serving its first Pennsylvania customer in 2013. Public utility materials describe Leatherstocking as the newest public utility in Pennsylvania in more than 40 years, with franchise territory in Susquehanna and Bradford counties and adjacent service territory in New York. The utility sits within the Corning and Argo ownership chain, but public sources do not disclose the current ownership percentages of the operating company.",
